{"id":"ahikam","name":"Ahikam","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:ahikam"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Ahikam","text":"Brother of support = helper, one of the five whom Josiah sent to consult the prophetess Huldah in connection with the discovery of the book of the law (2 Kings 22:12-14; 2 Chr. 34:20). He was the son of Shaphan, the royal secretary, and the father of Gedaliah, governor of Judea after the destruction of Jerusalem by the Babylonians (2 Kings 25:22; Jer. 40:5-16; 43:6). On one occasion he protected Jeremiah against the fury of Jehoiakim (Jer. 26:24). It was in the chamber of another son (Germariah) of Shaphan that Baruch read in the ears of all the people Jeremiah’s roll."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H296","lemma":"אֲחִיקָם","xlit":"ʼĂchîyqâm","gloss":"Achikam, an Israelite","kjv":"Ahikam","count":20,"share":0.53},{"strong":"H582","lemma":"אֱנוֹשׁ","xlit":"ʼĕnôwsh","gloss":"a man in general","kjv":"another, thirsty, certain, chap; divers","count":13,"share":0.34},{"strong":"H1121","lemma":"בֵּן","xlit":"bên","gloss":"a son , in the widest sense , etc.)","kjv":"afflicted, age, ite, ed one","count":30,"share":0.79},{"strong":"H7611","lemma":"שְׁאֵרִית","xlit":"shᵉʼêrîyth","gloss":"a remainder or residual portion","kjv":"that had escaped, be left, posterity, remain","count":4,"share":0.11},{"strong":"H6485","lemma":"פָּקַד","xlit":"pâqad","gloss":"to visit","kjv":"appoint, at all, avenge, bestow","count":7,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H2428","lemma":"חַיִל","xlit":"chayil","gloss":"probably a force, whether of men, means or other resources","kjv":"able, activity, army, band of men","count":5,"share":0.13}],"verses":["2Kgs.22.12","2Kgs.22.14","2Kgs.25.22","2Chr.34.20","Jer.26.24","Jer.39.14","Jer.40.5","Jer.40.6","Jer.40.7","Jer.40.9","Jer.40.11","Jer.40.14","Jer.40.16","Jer.41.1","Jer.41.2","Jer.41.6","Jer.41.10","Jer.41.16","Jer.41.18","Jer.43.6","2Kgs.22.13","Jer.40.8","Jer.40.10","Jer.40.12","Jer.40.13","Jer.40.15","